{"type":"npc","name":"Rothive","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":75,"temp":0,"max":75,"details":"void healing"},"ac":{"value":20,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":30,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":15}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"death-effects","exceptions":[]},{"type":"disease","exceptions":[]},{"type":"paralyzed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"poison","exceptions":[]},{"type":"swarm-mind","exceptions":[]},{"type":"unconscious","exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["necril"],"details":"Speak with wasps"},"level":{"value":4},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Rothives arise when flesh-eating wasps or bees infest a corpse suffused with void energy. Clerics of insect-related deities or wicked druids sometimes encourage the creation of rothives by collecting swarming insects and placing their queen in the mouth of a fresh corpse, then leaving it to slowly reanimate.</p><p>Rothives communicate through the hum of their insects, frequently singing about \"the Thrum\" and asserting their ability to carry out its commands. What the will of the Thrum entails remains a mystery, as most often the observable activities of rothives tend to be relegated to ambushing travelers in woodland areas or commanding swarms of wasps to descend on unsuspecting communities.</p><p>In the rare communities that deal with rothives regularly, beekeepers are respected for their ability to use their bee smokers in defense of their homes. There are stories of a beekeeper who sedated a rothive with smoke and spoke to them in the tongue of the dead, brokering a peaceful trading arrangement with the creature's Mother Hive. What is not often spoken of is the price the community has to pay to stay at peace or what terrible gifts the rothives bestow on them in return.</p><h2>Bees of a Feather</h2><p>Rothives are fascinated by mellifican hives and jealous of the psychic honey wasps' intelligence. Rothives that consume enough mellifican hives can eventually manifest new powers, granting them additional sonic damage or psychic abilities and increasing their overall power accordingly. These mellifican devourers are typically level 5 or 6, though rumors abound of ancient rothives who have grown to an even greater strength and intellect this way. These rothive masterminds hide in the shadows, manipulating other rothives for their own benefit.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 12/27/50 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), armor (light), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Diplomacy, Stealth, Survival)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> air, constitution, death, dexterity, energy resistant (void), mind, mind shield, poison, poisonous armor, sensory (darkvision), strength, throwing, unholy, wild, winged, wisdom</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Jameson Knopp","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":4},"dex":{"mod":2},"con":{"mod":4},"int":{"mod":-2},"wis":{"mod":2},"cha":{"mod":1}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":14,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":12,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":8,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":10,"special":[]},"athletics":{"base":12,"special":[]},"diplomacy":{"base":9,"special":[{"label":"to speak with wasps","predicate":["target:tag:wasp"],"base":11}]},"stealth":{"base":10,"special":[]},"survival":{"base":10,"special":[]}},"traits":{"value":["undead","unholy"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"med"}}},"_id":"HXxyZNQEUZEZKaho","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/rothive.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Rothive","displayName":0,"actorLi